<section>
  <h4>Defence in Depth</h4>
  <p>Scriptomatic applies multiple independent security layers so that a failure in any one layer does not expose the site.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Capability Gates — every save callback verifies <code>manage_options</code></li>
    <li>Dual Nonce Verification — both Settings API and per-location nonces must validate</li>
    <li>Input Validation — 100 KB cap, invalid UTF-8 rejected, dangerous HTML flagged</li>
    <li>URL Validation — external URLs validated with <code>wp_http_validate_url()</code></li>
    <li>Activity Logging — all saves, rollbacks, and file events recorded</li>
    <li>Open Redirect Hardening — post-action redirects use <code>admin_url()</code></li>
    <li>Singleton Guards — <code>__clone()</code> and <code>__wakeup()</code> prevent duplication</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section>
  <h4>Admin Pages</h4>
  <p>Four focused admin pages, each scoped to one location or purpose.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Head Scripts</strong> — inline JS editor, external URL manager, load conditions</li>
    <li><strong>Footer Scripts</strong> — same tools for the footer location</li>
    <li><strong>JS Files</strong> — create, edit, upload, and delete managed .js files</li>
    <li><strong>Preferences</strong> — log limit, API controls, email notifications</li>
  </ul>
</section>
